{#- Authentik (identity provider: login with password + passkey, forward auth
   for Caddy, OIDC for apps). Three containers, upstream compose layout:
   authentik-server (web/API on 9000, metrics on 9300), authentik-worker
   (background tasks, blueprints) and postgres. No Redis since 2025.10.
   All join the Podman network `network`, which formulas/caddy creates — so
   Caddy reaches http://authentik-server:9000 by name, nothing is published
   but metrics.

   Server and worker run as the image's own user (uid 1000 inside) in one
   user namespace (the worker joins the server's): data_dir (/data, media)
   and certs_dir (/certs) are handed to that mapping by :U, Salt only
   creates them — same pattern as netbox. postgres: image user 70:70, :U.

   Secrets (OpenBao via pillar): secret_key (`openssl rand 60 | base64 -w 0`)
   and pg_password. Written as files to secrets_dir (0700 dir, 0444 files)
   and bound into /run/secrets; Authentik reads them via file:// in its env,
   postgres via POSTGRES_PASSWORD_FILE — never in env or `podman inspect`.
   oidc_secrets: {<APP>: client secret} -> env HOMELAB_OIDC_<APP>_SECRET in  secret-scan: allow (doc text)
   the worker's secret env file, for OAuth2 provider blueprints (!Env).

   Blueprints (files/blueprints/*.yaml.j2) are rendered to blueprints_dir
   and mounted read-only on /blueprints/homelab in the worker, which applies
   them on change and hourly. Parameters:
     domain        zone of the apps (<name>.<domain>) and of the forward
                   auth cookie
     external_host Authentik's own URL (https://auth.<domain>)
     admin_group   group allowed through forward auth (and to the OIDC apps)
                   — the built-in superuser group by default, so akadmin and
                   whoever is added there by hand get in.

   oidc_apps: [{slug, name, redirect_uris, launch_url}] -> one OAuth2
   provider + application each (files/blueprints/50-oidc.yaml), client_id =
   slug, secret = oidc_secrets[slug] (required for every listed app).  secret-scan: allow (doc text)

   dump_dir: where formulas/backup's pre-run pg_dump goes; pillar/backup.sls
   repeats it and postgres_container_name.
   podman / worker_podman / postgres_podman: spec overrides (keys:
   formulas/podman README). #}
